   "title": "READ ME FIRST",
   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "## MiniMax H3 shot chain \u2014 one long animation from N shots\n\n**Costs API credits** (H3 is an API node; the price badge on the node\nshows per-shot cost). Needs a Comfy API key (Settings -> API).\n\n**Setup:** upload a start frame on *Load Image*, write your motion\nprompt on the H3 node, set **iterations** on Repeat Open to the number\nof shots.\n\nEach pass:\n1. \"value0\" carries the *current first frame* into H3.\n2. The generated shot is split into frames (Get Video Components).\n3. Its **last frame** (batch_index -1) becomes the next pass's first\n   frame -> seamless continuation.\n4. \"value1\" accumulates every shot's frames (Image Batch).\n\nAfter N passes, Repeat Close's value1 holds the full animation ->\nCreate Video -> Save Video.\n\nDetails:\n- The accumulator starts with your start frame, so the final video\n  leads with 1 still frame; trim it with *Get Image from Batch*\n  (batch_index 1, large length) if you care.\n- \"actual shot fps\" preview shows the fps of the first shot \u2014 set the\n  same value on Create Video.\n- The terminal logs every pass: \"[Repeat Open] pass 2 of 3 ...\" plus\n  per-node progress. Any miswiring fails with a message naming the\n  exact input to fix."
   ],
   "widgets_values_named": {
    "text": "## MiniMax H3 shot chain \u2014 one long animation from N shots\n\n**Costs API credits** (H3 is an API node; the price badge on the node\nshows per-shot cost). Needs a Comfy API key (Settings -> API).\n\n**Setup:** upload a start frame on *Load Image*, write your motion\nprompt on the H3 node, set **iterations** on Repeat Open to the number\nof shots.\n\nEach pass:\n1. \"value0\" carries the *current first frame* into H3.\n2. The generated shot is split into frames (Get Video Components).\n3. Its **last frame** (batch_index -1) becomes the next pass's first\n   frame -> seamless continuation.\n4. \"value1\" accumulates every shot's frames (Image Batch).\n\nAfter N passes, Repeat Close's value1 holds the full animation ->\nCreate Video -> Save Video.\n\nDetails:\n- The accumulator starts with your start frame, so the final video\n  leads with 1 still frame; trim it with *Get Image from Batch*\n  (batch_index 1, large length) if you care.\n- \"actual shot fps\" preview shows the fps of the first shot \u2014 set the\n  same value on Create Video.\n- The terminal logs every pass: \"[Repeat Open] pass 2 of 3 ...\" plus\n  per-node progress. Any miswiring fails with a message naming the\n  exact input to fix."
   },
   "color": "#432",
   "bgcolor": "#653"
  },
